<title>GERMANY: East German Sept industrial orders down 2.6 pct.</title>
<headline>East German Sept industrial orders down 2.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS    Sept 96     Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -2.6	 -3.6	-12.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+4.9	 -5.6	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		129.8	133.2	123.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				 Sept 96    Aug 96   Sept 96 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     -3.2	 +3.6     150.4</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with Jun/Jul 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  -7.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with Aug/Sept 95:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  -2.0</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +2.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 -21.6</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +8.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -16.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -0.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
